ARCHITECTURE

This folder documents tam-pane's system architecture: the modules and how
they connect, the data structures, the algorithms, the dependencies, and
the evaluations of other compositors that shaped them.


FILES

  principles.md          the design rules every change follows
  data-structures.md     Server, Monitor, Client, tags and the layout tree,
                         as they are built today
  dependencies.md        every library tam-pane uses, why, and which
                         version removes it
  mango-evaluation.md    how MangoWM works; what to take and what not to
                         repeat
  hyprland-evaluation.md the same for Hyprland

  Later phases add their own files here, for example lua-api.md (P2),
  ipc.md and protocols.md (P3).


KEEPING IT TRUE

  These documents describe the code as it is. A change that alters a
  structure, an algorithm or a dependency updates the matching file in
  the same commit. Where code and document disagree, the code is right
  and the document is a bug.
